{"name":"Wine Bottle","hex":"#d3d6c4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine bottle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall bottle with a long neck, normally made of dark or clear glass, for holding and serving wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine_bottle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine bottle","blocks":[{"text":"A wine bottle is a bottle, generally a glass bottle, that is used for holding wine. Some wines are fermented in the bottle while others are bottled only after fermentation. Recently the bottle has become a standard unit of volume to describe sales in the wine industry, measuring 750 millilitres. Wine bottles are produced, however, in a variety of volumes and shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Wine_bottle.JPG/330px-Wine_bottle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_bottle"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"},{"title":"Bottle","blocks":[{"text":"A bottle is a narrow-necked container made of an impermeable material in various shapes and sizes that stores and transports liquids. Its mouth, at the bottling line, can be sealed with an internal stopper, an external bottle cap, a closure, or induction sealing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Bouteille.jpg/330px-Bouteille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottle"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg/500px-Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg/1280px-Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg/500px-Paso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A square wine bottle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaso_Robles_red_blend_unique_wine_bottle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Veuve_clicquot_bottle_sizes.jpg/500px-Veuve_clicquot_bottle_sizes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Veuve_clicquot_bottle_sizes.jpg/500px-Veuve_clicquot_bottle_sizes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Side-by-side comparison of various sizes of champagne bottles (left to right), on the ladder: magnum, full, half, and quarter; on the floor: Balthazar, Salmanazar, Methuselah, and Jeroboam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeuve_clicquot_bottle_sizes.jpg"},